### 10. TYPES/INTERFACES FOR TASKS

All types come from `@kynetic-ai/shared` (at `/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/packages/shared/src/api.ts`):

```ts
interface TaskSummary {
    _ulid: string;
    slugs: string[];
    title: string;
    type: string;
    status: string;          // 'pending' | 'in_progress' | 'pending_review' | 'blocked' | 'completed' | 'cancelled'
    priority: number;        // 1 (highest) to N
    spec_ref?: string;
    tags: string[];
    depends_on: string[];
    created_at: string;
    started_at?: string;
    notes_count: number;
    todos_count?: number;
}

interface TaskDetail extends TaskSummary {
    derivation?: string;
    blocked_by: string[];
    depends_on: string[];
    context: string[];
    vcs_refs: string[];
    notes: Note[];
    todos?: Todo[];
}

interface Note {
    _ulid: string;
    created_at: string;
    author: string;
    content: string;
    supersedes?: string;
}

interface Todo {
    _ulid: string;
    content: string;
    status: 'pending' | 'in_progress' | 'completed';
    created_at: string;
}
```

### STATUS COLORS (used across multiple components)

These are defined inline as lookup objects in `TaskList.svelte`, `TaskDetailPanel.svelte`, `TaskDetail.svelte`, `ItemDetail.svelte`, and the tasks `+page.svelte`:

```ts
const statusColors: Record<string, string> = {
    pending: 'bg-gray-500',
    in_progress: 'bg-blue-500',
    pending_review: 'bg-yellow-500',
    blocked: 'bg-red-500',
    completed: 'bg-green-500',
    cancelled: 'bg-gray-400'
};
```

The dashboard page uses a slightly different variant:
```ts
{ key: 'ready', color: 'bg-green-500' }       // "Ready" = pending without unmet deps
{ key: 'in_progress', color: 'bg-blue-500' }
{ key: 'pending_review', color: 'bg-yellow-500' }
{ key: 'blocked', color: 'bg-red-500' }
{ key: 'completed', color: 'bg-gray-500' }
```

Priority colors (in TaskList):
```ts
priority === 1: 'text-red-600 font-bold'
priority === 2: 'text-orange-600 font-semibold'
priority === 3: 'text-yellow-600'
default: 'text-gray-600'
```

Spec item type colors (in ItemTree):
```ts
module: 'bg-purple-500'
feature: 'bg-blue-500'
requirement: 'bg-green-500'
trait: 'bg-yellow-500'
```

Observation type colors (in observations page):
```ts
friction: 'text-red-600'
success: 'text-green-600'
question: 'text-blue-600'
idea: 'text-yellow-600'
```

Triage action colors:
```ts
promote: 'bg-green-500'
delete: 'bg-red-500'
defer: 'bg-yellow-500'
'spec-gap': 'bg-purple-500'
duplicate: 'bg-gray-500'
```

**Important note:** These color mappings are **duplicated** across multiple files -- there is no centralized design token or utility for status/type colors.

### SVELTE 5 PATTERNS SUMMARY

| Pattern | Where Used |
|---------|------------|
| `$state` | All stores (connection, mode, project), all page components, task detail panel |
| `$derived` | `ConnectionStatus` (state/label), `CommandPalette` (groupedResults), `TaskFilters` (URL params), `Sidebar` (showProjectSelector), triage page (filteredItems, currentItem, allTags, progress counts) |
| `$derived.by()` | `ConnectionStatus` (variant, label), sidebar context (open, state), triage page (allItems, filteredItems) |
| `$effect` | Dashboard (project version reload), tasks page (filter params, project version, URL ref), CommandPalette (debounced search), items page (URL ref), triage page (filter reset, project version) |
| `$effect.pre` | data-table.svelte.ts (table options update) |
| `$props()` | Layout, TaskDetailPanel, TaskDetail, all shadcn-svelte ui components |
| `$bindable` | TaskDetailPanel (open, task), badge (ref), button (ref) |
| `{#snippet}` / `{@render}` | Layout (`children`), CommandPalette, ItemTree (recursive `renderNode`), sidebar menu button (`child`), all shadcn-svelte components |
| `flushSync` | Tasks page (panel open synchronous update) |

### BITS-UI COMPONENTS USED

The shadcn-svelte components wrap `bits-ui` (v2.15.4). These bits-ui primitives are used:
- **Accordion** (AccordionItem, AccordionTrigger, AccordionContent)
- **Badge** (custom implementation with tailwind-variants)
- **Button** (custom with tailwind-variants)
- **Card** (CardHeader, CardContent, CardFooter, CardTitle, CardDescription, CardAction)
- **Command** (CommandDialog, CommandInput, CommandList, CommandGroup, CommandItem, CommandEmpty, CommandLoading, CommandSeparator, CommandShortcut, CommandLinkItem)
- **Dialog** (DialogContent, DialogHeader, DialogTitle, DialogDescription, DialogFooter, DialogClose, DialogOverlay, DialogPortal, DialogTrigger)
- **Input** (custom)
- **Select** (SelectTrigger, SelectContent, SelectItem, SelectGroup, SelectGroupHeading, SelectLabel, SelectPortal, SelectSeparator, SelectScrollUpButton, SelectScrollDownButton)
- **Separator** (custom)
- **Sheet** (SheetContent, SheetHeader, SheetTitle, SheetDescription, SheetFooter, SheetClose, SheetOverlay, SheetPortal, SheetTrigger)
- **Sidebar** (full component suite: Provider, Content, Footer, Group, Header, Menu, MenuItem, MenuButton, etc.)
- **Skeleton** (custom)
- **Table** (TableBody, TableRow, TableCell, TableHead, TableHeader, TableCaption, TableFooter)
- **Tabs** (TabsList, TabsTrigger, TabsContent)
- **Textarea** (custom)
- **Tooltip** (TooltipProvider, TooltipTrigger, TooltipContent, TooltipPortal)

Also includes **data-table** wrappers using `@tanstack/table-core` with `createSvelteTable()`.

